## What it does

A skill bundle is a set of skill documents and their companion files. The site builds one bundle from `skills/`. The site and workspace CLI read the same generated asset.

- The [discovery index](/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json) still lists the site's skill pages.
- The [Executor index](/.well-known/agent-skills/executor/index.json) describes the portable bundle. Supply that full URL to Executor's `wellKnownSkills` loader.
- The workspace CLI's `mcp` command and the site's [MCP](/lore/mcp-is-another-surface) endpoint serve the portable bundle through the Skills extension.
- The published `ratstack` npm command still serves only learn tools.
- The portable bundle omits `security-audit`. Its `HUNTING.md` workflow and reproduction guidance can help agents develop exploits.

## The standard

The original index keeps the agentskills.io discovery shape. Its `Link` header points to the Executor index as an alternate.

Each Executor entry lists `SKILL.md` first, then its companion paths. Every path resolves under the entry's named directory beside the index. The version is a SHA-256 digest of the ordered paths and their contents.

[SEP-2640](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/pull/2640) defines how MCP clients list skills and read their resources. Each manifest records a SHA-256 digest for each file. Each digest hashes the exact bytes both servers serve.

## How to check

Fetch the index and one skill:

```sh
curl -fsS https://ratstack.sh/.well-known/agent-skills/executor/index.json
curl -fsS https://ratstack.sh/.well-known/agent-skills/executor/durability/SKILL.md
```

The client must support the Skills extension. Use this server URL:

```text
https://ratstack.sh/mcp
```

1. Call `skills/list`.
2. Call `skills/get` with `skill://rat-stack/durability/SKILL.md`.
3. Call `resources/read` with that URI. Compute the SHA-256 of the returned text and compare it with the manifest's `digest`.

For the workspace CLI, build before connecting the same client over standard input and output:

```sh
pnpm turbo run build --filter=@rat-stack/cli --summarize
node apps/cli/dist/cli.js mcp
```
